REQP-1839#1 Warning
RAMB36 async control check  
The RAMB36E1 i_sram/memory_reg_1 has an input control pin i_sram/memory_reg_1/ADDRARDADDR[14] (net: i_sram/addr_i[10]) which is driven by a register (i_node/i_core/i_cpu/core_i/cs_registers_i/gen_trigger_regs.tmatch_value_q_reg[0]) that has an active asychronous set or reset. This may cause corruption of the memory contents and/or read values when the set/reset is asserted and is not analyzed by the default static timing analysis. It is suggested to eliminate the use of a set/reset to registers driving this RAMB pin or else use a synchronous reset in which the assertion of the reset is timed by default.
